1. What Is Systems Engineering?

Systems Engineering (SE) is a multidisciplinary approach used to define, develop, integrate, verify, and manage complex systems throughout their entire lifecycle. It ensures that all system components work together effectively to meet stakeholder and customer needs.

A Systems Engineer is responsible for:

Defining and managing system requirements
Ensuring compatibility and integration among subsystems
Maintaining alignment with customer and stakeholder expectations
Coordinating verification and validation activities
Managing system performance, risk, and technical interfaces

Example: Missile System Development
In the development of a missile system:

Mechanical Engineers design the structure, airframe, and mechanical components.

Electrical Engineers design the power systems, electronics, and circuitry.

Software Engineers develop the guidance, control, and mission software.

