17. Common Interview Questions
What is Systems Engineering?
"Systems Engineering is the discipline responsible for defining requirements, coordinating subsystem development, managing integration, and verifying that the final system meets customer needs."

Difference Between Verification and Validation?

"Verification asks whether we built the system correctly according to requirements. Validation asks whether we built the correct system for the customer's needs."

What is Integration Testing?

"Integration testing verifies that multiple components or subsystems interact correctly when combined into a larger system."

Why is Traceability Important?

"Traceability links requirements to design, implementation, and testing so that changes can be analyzed and every requirement can be verified."